              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page4_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Why does a methodology section need explicit inclusion/exclusion criteria rather than just \"patients\" or \"students\"?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "It's a formatting requirement with no real analytical purpose",
              "It defines exactly who the findings do and don't apply to, and lets someone else replicate the sample"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Precise criteria define the boundaries of your population and are essential for anyone trying to interpret or replicate your findings."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Measures and Instruments",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "State exactly what tools you're using to collect data \u2014 no detail is too small to specify."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Clinical chart review:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " name the EMR system explicitly (e.g., ARIA, Mosaiq) and the exact data points extracted (e.g., \"bladder volume in cc from the daily CBCT registration tab\")."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Educational survey:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " name the software (e.g., Qualtrics), the question types, and the validated instrument used if applicable (e.g., the STAI for anxiety)."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Vague instrumentation is one of the most common reasons a methodology section gets sent back for revision."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Putting the Full Proposal Together",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A complete research proposal typically includes, in order:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "orderedList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Problem statement and PICO question"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Brief literature review establishing the gap"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Research design and rationale for choosing it"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Purpose statement"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Participants, with inclusion/exclusion criteria"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Measures and instruments"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Analysis plan, tied to your variables' NOIR levels"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Ethics considerations and anticipated IRB pathway"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Notice this is just the earlier lessons in this section, assembled in the order a reader needs to encounter them \u2014 nothing new to invent here, just organizing what you've already built."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Presenting Your Work",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Whether you're presenting to a department quality-improvement meeting, a poster session, or a formal committee, the same discipline applies: lead with the problem and why it matters, state your question and design plainly, show your key result, and be direct about limitations. A three-sentence plain-language summary for a non-statistical audience is often harder to write than the full technical write-up \u2014 and usually more useful."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've covered writing a purpose statement, defining participants with inclusion/exclusion criteria, specifying measures and instruments, assembling a full proposal structure, and presenting findings to different audiences."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "That completes the research process from first observation to a finished, presentable project \u2014 you can revisit any lesson in this section independently whenever a specific step is what you need."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
